{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian has issued corrections to several articles that contained inaccuracies. The corrections were published to address errors that had been brought to their attention.\n\n***\nSection 2\nSome of the corrections include clarifying that a new law making the abduction of a cat or dog a specific criminal offence applies to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK. Other corrections include: \n* The correct title and role of Eileen Burbidge, who is the executive director of Fertifa, not the founder.\n* Corrections to an interview with Juliet Stevenson, where the director's name was misspelled as \"Lowther\" instead of \"Lawther\".\n\nSection 3\nThe corrections also addressed other errors, such as the incorrect identification of the family in the film Bend It Like Beckham as Muslim instead of Sikh, and the incorrect statement that Venetia Stanley's father had converted to Islam. The Guardian has provided contact information for readers to reach out to the Readers' Editor with any concerns or feedback.\n\nSection 4\nReaders can contact the Readers' Editor by writing to the Observer, York Way, London N1 9GU, or by emailing observer.readers@observer.co.uk, or by calling 020 3353 4736. \nP.P.S The corrections demonstrate the Guardian's commitment to accuracy and transparency in their reporting.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -2.8013790142722428e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Guardian", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " has", "logprob": -0.1049228385090828}, {"token": " issued", "logprob": -0.0018442542059347034}, {"token": " corrections", "logprob": -0.029